% refs-held.bib — verified bibliography entries not yet cited by the manuscript.
%
% Nothing reads this file. finishing/tools/refs_ledger.py, check_typography.py and
% the build all read finishing/refs.bib and only that, so an entry parked here is
% inert: it does not enter the ledger, it is not counted in the footer's entry
% total, and it does not reach the printed bibliography.
%
% Why entries wait here. The book has no \nocite, so an entry nothing cites never
% prints. Merging one into refs.bib would raise the count in every page footer
% above the number of works in the References, and the record's standing claim
% that every entry is cited would stop being true. So an entry arrives here when
% it has been verified but the edit that cites it has not arrived, and moves to
% refs.bib in the same commit as that edit.
%
% These ten came with the D-359 instruction set, whose items 7, 10, 12–16 and
% 18–22 did not arrive. Every field below was verified on 2026-09-18, by Crossref
% where a DOI exists and against publisher or library records otherwise; the
% notes record what was checked and the two places a supplied field was wrong.
% The `checked` column of the bibliography ledger means a HUMAN check and none of
% these has had one.
%
% One thing to expect on merging: of these ten entries' authors, names_guard.py
% finds exactly one on the persona roster, so singer2014empathy will produce a
% single warn-level hit for a human to confirm is a citation. That is the guard
% working as designed and not a violation.

